{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#def:dc-ch3-expmap","title":"def:dc-ch3-expmap","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.md","line":268,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex#def:dc-ch3-expmap","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods.tex","label":"def:dc-ch3-expmap","line":753,"source":"\\begin{definition}[exponential map]\n  \\label{def:dc-ch3-expmap}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist, lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique}\n\n  \\dcref{ch3:after-2.8}\n  The \\emph{exponential map} at $p\\in M$ is $\\exp_p(v)=\\gamma(1,p,v)$, the value at\n  time $1$ of the (maximal) geodesic with initial data $(p,v)$; its natural\n  domain is the set of $v\\in T_pM$ whose maximal geodesic is defined at time\n  $1$, which always contains $0$, and $\\exp_p(0)=p$.\n\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[exponential map] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a64632d6368332d6578706d6170\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-5-exist\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods%23lem%3Adc-ch3-2-5-unique\">↗ lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:after-2.8</span></span>The <em>exponential map</em> at <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> is <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p(v)=\\gamma (1,p,v)$\">$\\exp _p(v)=\\gamma (1,p,v)$</span>, the value at time <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span> of the (maximal) geodesic with initial data <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(p,v)$\">$(p,v)$</span>; its natural domain is the set of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$v\\in T_pM$\">$v\\in T_pM$</span> whose maximal geodesic is defined at time <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$1$\">$1$</span>, which always contains <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0$\">$0$</span>, and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\exp _p(0)=p$\">$\\exp _p(0)=p$</span>. <p></p>","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#rem:dc-ch3-2-8","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-exist"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-5-unique"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","title":"lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray","label":"lem:dc-ch3-expmap-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch03_GeodesicsConvexNeighborhoods#lem:dc-ch3-2-9-strict","title":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-strict","label":"lem:dc-ch3-2-9-strict"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blue